# xdplus system-side init additions.

# The prebuilt 8.1 vendor configstore service SIGSYS-crashes on its stale
# seccomp policy and restart-loops forever (log noise, wasted cycles). The
# system-side android.hardware.configstore@1.1-service.xdplus replaces it
# (see device configstore/), so stop the vendor copy once boot completes.
on property:sys.boot_completed=1
    stop configstore-hal-1-0

# Vendor HAL services started from the 8.1 vendor rc can lose the boot race
# against hwservicemanager: the process stays alive but its interface never
# registers, and (VINTF unenforced) clients block forever in getService().
# Seen with configstore (replaced above) and light@2.0 (system_server thread
# hung on ILight). Kick the known victims once the manager is ready.
on property:hwservicemanager.ready=true
    restart light-hal-2-0
